* Tue Nov 17 2026 Steven Pritchard <steve@sicura.us> - 0.4.0
- Publish as `simp-nm`, a fork of `lsst-nm` 0.3.0. The `nm` class and the
  `nm::connection` defined type keep their names and parameters.
- Restart NetworkManager when `NetworkManager.conf` changes
- Allow puppet/extlib 8.x
- Add `nm::connection` parameters `activate` and `connection_id`, to apply a
  changed profile to an active connection (off by default)
- Add `nm::connection` parameter `replaces_ifcfg`, to remove the `ifcfg` file
  for the same device (off by default)
- Require puppetlabs/stdlib 9 or later, for `stdlib::ensure_packages`
- Allow puppetlabs/stdlib 10.x
- Support EL 8, 9 and 10 (RedHat, CentOS Stream, AlmaLinux, Rocky, OracleLinux)
- Require OpenVox 8 or 9 (replaces the `puppet` requirement)
- Drop support for CentOS 7
- **BREAKING** (relative to `lsst-nm`): `nm::purge_connections` now defaults to
  `false`. Set it to `true` to remove unmanaged connection profiles.
- **BREAKING** (relative to `lsst-nm`): `/etc/sysconfig/network-scripts` is no
  longer managed or purged. Set the new `nm::purge_ifcfg` to `true` to purge it.
- **BREAKING** (relative to `lsst-nm`): `/etc/NetworkManager/conf.d` is no
  longer managed or purged. Set the new `nm::purge_conf_d` to `true` to purge it.
- **BREAKING** (relative to `lsst-nm`): `NetworkManager.conf` is no longer
  managed unless `nm::conf` is set, and setting it takes ownership of the
  whole file. To restore the old default, set `nm::conf` to
  `{main: {}, logging: {}}`.

* Sat Dec 02 2023 Joshua Hoblitt <josh@hoblitt.com> - 0.3.0
